description: Hackathon boundaries and quality bar
alwaysApply: true
---
# Boundaries
- This repo is PUBLIC and standalone. Never import from, copy, or reference private Ive code, prompts, configs, or keys.
- Everything here must be NEW work written during the hackathon. If reuse of anything pre-existing is unavoidable, stop and ask me; don't do it silently.
- Never commit secrets. Use env vars; keep .env.example current.

# Meta API
- Do not guess model IDs, endpoints, or request shapes. Read https://dev.meta.ai/docs/quickstart, /docs/models, and https://github.com/meta-models/meta-model-cookbook first. If you cannot verify something, say so and ask.
- Put every Meta call behind an adapter in src/meta_client with typed inputs/outputs, retries, timeouts, and usage logging (tokens, latency, cost).
- Use Standard mode, not Contributor mode.

# Quality
- Every module has a runnable example and tests for the failure paths.
- Anything that produces numbers (evals) must be reproducible: fixed seeds, saved raw outputs in ivebench/results/.
- Small commits with clear messages. Update HACKATHON_SCOPE.md when a module is added.
- Don't add features outside the current task.
